## Notes

- `name`, `disk_path`, `disk_size_mb`, `storage_controller`, `iso_path`, and
  `iso_controller` are immutable — changing any of them replaces the virtual
  machine. Only `os_type`, `memory`, `cpus`, and `vram` are updated in place (the
  VM is powered off and back on if it was running).
- Disks cannot be resized in place. Increasing `disk_size_mb` recreates the
  virtual machine, which destroys the existing disk.
- VirtualBox normalizes some `os_type` values (for example `Other` is reported as
  `Other/Unknown`). The provider preserves your configured value so this does not
  show up as a perpetual diff.
- When one or more `network_adapter` blocks are present, the provider manages all
  eight adapters (`nic1`–`nic8`) and disables any not listed. Omit the block
  entirely to keep VirtualBox's default NAT adapter. Adapter changes are applied
  in place (the VM is powered off and back on if it was running).
- `disk_image` clones the source image to a per-VM disk with a fresh UUID, so each
  VM — including every `for_each` instance — gets its own writable copy and the
  source image is never modified. It is mutually exclusive with `disk_size_mb`.

